# Module structure

Each module under `src/modules/{module}/`:

```
domain/          # Aggregates, VOs, domain services, port interfaces — pure, no framework
application/     # Commands, queries, event handlers — orchestrates domain
infrastructure/  # Prisma repos, external adapters — implements ports
```

## Layer constraints

- **Domain & application:** strict TypeScript, no `any`, no Prisma, no Next.js, no next-intl
- **Infrastructure only:** Prisma, Clerk adapters, external APIs
- **Identity:** Clerk lives behind an anti-corruption layer; only `UserId` crosses module boundaries

## Testing (co-located in module)

| Level | Scope | Rule |
|-------|-------|------|
| Unit | `domain/` | Vitest, no DB/network/framework; cover every invariant |
| Integration | `application/` | Vitest + real PostgreSQL, no mocks |
| E2E | — | Playwright in `tests/e2e/` |

## Before adding code

1. Confirm the concept belongs in this module (`docs/product/modules.md`)
2. Confirm aggregates/Vos match `docs/product/domain-model.md`
3. Expose cross-module access via application services or events — not repositories
